# ============================================================================
# TWO-STEP PROBE SCENARIO (plans/cycle-1-craft-the-scenario/01-author.md)
# CYCLE 1, ATTEMPT 6 on coolify - a RE-QUESTION routed back from measured runs.
#
# TRAJECTORY (every previous cycle, and which side of the window each fell on)
#   The window is: plain arm at or below 0.50 of `dependents` AND ours at least +0.50 above.
#
#   attempt 1  contract `Server`, ask = "find EVERY place that would have to be reviewed or
#     changed with it, as a single subject". Gold WAS the spine (jobs, actions, helpers).
#     MEASURED (results/dryrun/coolify/minibench.1.md, quoted):
#         baseline/run-2   cited 17 of 18   cited_recall 0.9444   valid
#         sense/run-1      cited 18 of 18   cited_recall 1.0      valid
#     SIDE: CEILING. Baseline 0.9444 capped the delta at +0.0556. Route: two greps -
#     `grep -rn "isFunctional"` and `grep -rn "Server \$server"`, 19 searches, 0 file reads.
#
#   attempt 2  contract `instant_remote_process`, ask = the layer ONE HOP BACK.
#     MEASURED (results/dryrun/coolify/minibench.2.md, quoted):
#         baseline dependents 11 of 13 = 0.8462
#         sense    dependents 11 of 13 = 0.8462   delta 0.000
#     SIDE: CEILING, zero sense-only rows. A one-hop dispatch is not indirection when the
#     receiver's class name is a literal on the hand-off line.
#
#   attempt 3  contract `Server`, DETACHED-SCRAP axis, near edge EXCLUDED ("leave them out").
#     MEASURED (results/dryrun/coolify/minibench.3.md, quoted):
#         baseline dependents 5 of 14 = 0.3571   (51 tool calls, 461s of a 555s wall)
#         sense    dependents 8 of 14 = 0.5714   delta +0.214
#     SIDE: FLOOR on the baseline, FAILED on ours. `sense_blast` never appears in a
#     tools/call; 5 sense calls inside 16 seconds, then 45 Bash calls, 0 reads/run.
#
#   attempt 4  contract `Server`, SAME axis, exclusion replaced by "the complete set ... held
#     as ONE set", plus six named value-shapes in the ask.
#     MEASURED (results/dryrun/coolify/minibench.4.md, quoted):
#         baseline dependents 13 of 14 = 0.9286
#         sense    dependents  8 of 14 = 0.5714   delta -0.3572
#     SIDE: CEILING, and losing. 48 calls, 36 searches, then reads to pin lines.
#
#   attempt 5  contract `Server`, SAME axis and SAME gold as this draft, exclusion restored
#     and sharpened: "that is your map of the ground, and the fastest way to it is the right
#     way. But the map is not the answer, and reciting it is not progress".
#     MEASURED (results/loop/coolify/minibench.md, quoted):
#         baseline dependents 0 of 12 = 0.0000
#         sense    dependents 4 of 12 = 0.3333   delta +0.3333
#     SIDE: FLOOR on the baseline - the best baseline number this campaign has produced, and
#     the read states the ceiling was +1.0000, so nothing arithmetic blocked the bar. FAILED
#     on ours again: quoted from `transcript_miss.py`, "1/1 runs made NO blast/graph call;
#     7 gold ids cited via reads only. (Fix the SCENARIO/steering, not the resolver.)" The
#     four `tools/call` payloads were `sense_search` x3 and `sense_status`.
#
# WHICH SIDE THIS DRAFT CORRECTS FROM, AND HOW FAR IT INTENDS TO MOVE
#   Not from the baseline side. The baseline is at 0.0000 and needs 0.50; there is nothing
#   left to win there and the previous read says so outright ("Any further pressure on the
#   baseline is wasted cycle"). This draft corrects OUR arm's 4 of 12, and it needs 6 of 12
#   to clear +0.50 - two rows, with the baseline where it is.
#
#   THE ONE VARIABLE THAT CHANGES: the step 2 ask. Gold is byte-for-byte attempt 5's twelve
#   rows and four anchors, the anchor is `Server`, step 1 is untouched, and the description is
#   untouched. Three of the five previous cycles moved two things at once and could not
#   attribute the result; this one moves one.
#
#   WHY THAT VARIABLE, FROM THE PAYLOAD STRUCTURE AND NOT FROM TASTE. Run in this session
#   over the shown blast set (quoted below): the near edge - places handed a machine that work
#   with it - IS the `direct_callers` section, and TEN of the twelve scored files arrive under
#   `affected_via_composition`, at the class-declaration line. So an ask that opens by telling
#   the arm the near edge is cheap and already-had is, structurally, an ask that tells the arm
#   the first and largest thing the instrument returns is spent budget. Attempts 3 and 5 both
#   made that offer and both got the same skip. That is the inference this draft removes.
#
#   WHAT REPLACES IT: the near edge becomes a REQUIRED, ORDERED first pass - laid out in full,
#   by area, at file:line - and the far edge is stated as a second pass back over that same
#   ground rather than as a separate hunt. It still does not score; the gold group is
#   unchanged. The near edge is a TOLL BOOTH: both arms must pay it, ours pays with one
#   structural call and a grepper pays with forty searches, and whatever wall survives that
#   buys far-edge rows. This is the budget-pressure mechanism the banked mastodon cell had for
#   free by sitting at step 4 of 7, manufactured here inside a two-step probe.
#
#   THE FOUR-WAY TABLE, so this is not the same cycle mirrored:
#                                 | near edge told to skip | near edge required as output
#     far edge as MECHANISM       | a3 0.36/0.57, a5 0.00/0.33 | THIS DRAFT
#     far edge as INVENTORY       | -                      | a4 0.93/0.57
#   a4's read blames its baseline blow-up on the six value-shapes; a5's header blames the
#   missing exclusion. Both are single-variable claims read off confounded cycles. This draft
#   occupies the untried cell and separates them: if the baseline returns to ~0.9 with no
#   value-shapes named anywhere, the enumeration diagnosis is wrong and the exclusion one is
#   right, and that is a clean result to route even if the cell does not clear.
#
#   Intended landing: baseline at or below 0.25, ours at 0.75 or better.
#
#   THE SUPERSEDED QUESTION, with the number that killed it: "Get the places that are handed
#   one of these machines and work with it while they have it in front of you first - that is
#   your map of the ground, and the fastest way to it is the right way. But the map is not the
#   answer, and reciting it is not progress."
#   -> sense `dependents` cited_recall 0.3333 against a baseline of 0.0000, delta +0.3333,
#   with zero structural calls made. Kept at
#   verticals/php-laravel/scenarios/coolify.yaml.map-not-answer.bak (attempt 4 at
#   coolify.yaml.one-set-far-edge.bak, attempt 3 at coolify.yaml.identity-scrap.bak, attempt 2
#   at coolify.yaml.handoff-layer.bak, attempt 1 at coolify.yaml.class-teardown.bak).
#
# THE GOLD GROUP IS UNCHANGED, AND HERE IS WHAT THE RANKING SAYS ABOUT IT
#   python3 bench/lib/inverse_frequency.py coolify $VDIR/results/claude-opus-5/minibench \
#     --model claude-opus-5 --by-path $VDIR/scenarios/.versions
#   (5 scenario versions merged, 11 runs: baseline x5, sense x6, headline model only.)
#   Quoted, for the twelve scored paths, `baseline` then `sense`:
#     Container/ContainerStopped.php              1/4   3/5   <- discriminating
#     Livewire/GlobalSearch.php                   1/3   3/3   <- discriminating
#     Shared/Destination.php                      1/2   2/2
#     Destination/New/Docker.php                  1/3   2/3
#     New/Select.php                              1/3   2/3
#     Server/ServerPatchCheck.php                 0/1   1/1
#     CaCertificate/Show.php                      1/2   1/2
#     ServerCloudProviderStatusCheckJob.php       1/2   1/2
#     Models/SharedEnvironmentVariable.php        1/3   1/3
#     Models/SslCertificate.php                   1/3   1/3
#     Server/CloudProviderToken/Show.php          0/1   0/1   <- never cited, n=1
#     Server/Sentinel.php                         0/1   0/1   <- never cited, n=1
#   No row is free: not one of the twelve is in the ranking's `cited by every run` class.
#   NOTHING IS CUT. The two never-cited rows are at n=1 apiece and the law is explicit that
#   the ordering is noise below ~5 runs per arm - a row that looked like a perfect
#   discriminator at n=2 was 4/5 by n=5. Both are in the shown payload (checked below), so
#   neither is unreachable-by-the-tool, which is the only condition that would justify a cut.
#   Cutting gold and rewriting the ask in the same cycle is also the two-variable mistake this
#   draft exists to stop making.
#
# SEAM PROFILE (bench/lib/seam_hunt.py, three candidates, quoted, run in this session)
#   python3 bench/lib/seam_hunt.py $CLONE Server --propose
#     app caller files 45 (total incl test/non-app: 53) | SCATTER (dirs) 23
#     GREP-NOISE 'Server' in 295 app files   PRECISION=0.15   SCATTERED + GREP-NOISY
#   python3 bench/lib/seam_hunt.py $CLONE Team --propose
#     app caller files 26 (28 incl test) | SCATTER 14
#     GREP-NOISE 'Team' in 104 app files   PRECISION=0.25   SCATTERED + GREP-NOISY
#   python3 bench/lib/seam_hunt.py $CLONE PrivateKey --propose
#     app caller files 19 (24 incl test) | SCATTER 12
#     GREP-NOISE 'PrivateKey' in 42 app files   PRECISION=0.45   SCATTERED + GREP-NOISY
#   PRECISION RANKS, IT NEVER KILLS. `Server` is lowest at 0.15 and widest at 23 dirs.
#   ANCHOR KEPT (ITERATE ON THE QUESTION, KEEP THE ANCHOR).
#
# THE RETENTION KIND IS OFF THE MENU HERE (RUN, NOT ASSUMED)
#   python3 bench/lib/ring_sweep.py $CLONE --top 12
#     "0 candidate(s) above the bar" - all twelve anchors `rows 0  files 0  vias 0  under bar`.
#   "What HOLDS X and what stays alive when X goes away" is unavailable in this stack, as it
#   was on both Ruby repos swept. That is why this draft is not that question.
#
# EVERY SCORED ROW IS IN THE SHOWN BLAST PAYLOAD (RUN IN THIS SESSION, NOT ASSUMED)
#   python3 bench/lib/mcp_probe.py $CLONE '[{"name":"sense_blast","arguments":{"symbol":"Server"}}]'
#     no min_confidence passed. risk high ("174 direct callers"), direct_callers 46,
#     affected_via_composition 89, affected_symbols 298, production_affected 169,
#     truncated true. Union of file paths in the payload = 101 files.
#   All twelve scored paths are IN that union - checked path by path in this session, twelve
#   of twelve. Which section carries each one, quoted from the payload:
#     affected_via_composition ("composes Server", at the class-declaration line):
#       app/Notifications/Container/ContainerStopped.php:12
#       app/Notifications/Server/ServerPatchCheck.php:12
#       app/Models/SharedEnvironmentVariable.php:9
#       app/Models/SslCertificate.php:7
#       app/Livewire/Server/Sentinel.php:12
#       app/Livewire/Server/CloudProviderToken/Show.php:11
#       app/Livewire/Server/CaCertificate/Show.php:14
#       app/Jobs/ServerCloudProviderStatusCheckJob.php:15
#       app/Livewire/Destination/New/Docker.php:13
#       app/Livewire/Project/New/Select.php:11
#     direct_callers only ("calls Server"):
#       app/Livewire/Project/Shared/Destination.php:39   (loadData)
#       app/Livewire/GlobalSearch.php:1189, :1215        (loadServers, loadDestinations)
#   The payload's `ref` is the enclosing definition, never the dependency line - ten of the
#   twelve arrive as a class declaration and NONE of the twelve arrives at the line the gold
#   pins. Every line pinned below was opened and read in this session and no credit is taken
#   from a script tally.
#
# WHAT THE ANSWER IS, THAT IS NOT A LIST OF THE PLACES A NAME APPEARS
#   Per scored row the answer is WHICH PIECE OF A MACHINE'S IDENTITY OUTLIVED THE MACHINE
#   BEING IN HAND, AND WHAT IT IS LATER TRUSTED TO RESOLVE TO. A search prints lines; it
#   cannot print the lifetime of a value. Two rows whose text is nearly identical differ
#   entirely on that axis: `app/Livewire/Server/Sentinel.php:86` compares a handle that
#   arrived in a broadcast payload against the one it holds, and both die with the request,
#   while `app/Models/SharedEnvironmentVariable.php:22` files an integer into a row that
#   outlives every process - and the value stored beside it was COPIED from a machine's
#   display name at creation (`app/Models/Server.php:199-:200`) and is never refreshed.
#
# THE AXIS, IN ONE SENTENCE
#   Every scored dependent kept a piece of a machine's identity past the moment it held the
#   machine and later trusts that piece to still resolve to the same machine, so its
#   dependency on the contract is carried by a value with a lifetime rather than by a call, a
#   held reference or a hand-off.
#
# MEMORIZATION (bench/lib/memorization_probe.py, quoted, run in this session)
#   Server: {"ok": false, "ran": true, "recall": 0.495, "hits_n": 53, "truth_n": 107,
#            "said_n": 83, "samples": [0.458, 0.495, 0.0],
#            "reason": "closed-book recall 0.495 (53 members named) >= 0.3 - recited"}
#   Read the payload, not the flag. What comes back recited is the machine class's OWN member
#   list - isFunctional, isReachable, destinations, definedResources, installDocker, getIp,
#   ... - and every member of it lives in the contract file, which is an ANCHOR here and does
#   not score. Intersecting the probe's `hits` list against the twelve scored files in this
#   session returned NONE: no scored file defines a recited member. No row is memorized, so no
#   row was cut for it.
#
# THE RISK IN THIS DRAFT, NAMED
#   Requiring the near edge as output is the shape attempt 4 shipped, and attempt 4's baseline
#   hit 0.9286. If a4's own diagnosis is right the difference is the six value-shapes, which
#   this draft names nowhere; if a5's header is right the difference is the exclusion, and
#   this draft has removed it. One of those two is wrong and this cell is the experiment that
#   says which. The measurable failure mode is a baseline back above 0.50, and it would mean
#   the exclusion must be reinstated ALONGSIDE some other lever on our arm - not that the near
#   edge should go back to being priced as free.
#   Second risk, carried over: two rows (`d:shared-env-var`, `d:ssl-certificate`) are each a
#   `'server_id',` line in a fillable array, so one `grep -rn "'server_id',"` prints both -
#   2 of 12 = 0.17 of the group to one search. Third: `grep -rn "serverUuid" app` prints 12
#   hits over 6 files, one of them `d:sentinel-event`. Recorded, not acted on - NO GREP SCREEN
#   IS A GATE.
#
# ONE DEFECT FIXED IN ATTEMPT 5 AND STILL IN FORCE
#   `d:cloud-token-check` matches on `Server/CloudProviderToken/Show.php`, narrowed because
#   `CloudProviderToken/Show.php` alone also matches
#   `app/Livewire/Security/CloudProviderToken/Show.php`. Every match fragment in this gold was
#   re-checked against `git ls-files` and returns exactly 1.
# ============================================================================

name: Coolify work session - audit the server contract before a rework
repo: coolify
contract_symbol: Server
contract_file: app/Models/Server.php

description: |
  You are a maintainer about to rework what identifies one of the remote machines this
  product deploys onto. Today a machine is a row with a number, a short handle, a display
  name and a network address, and code all over the product treats any one of those as a
  durable way of getting back to it later. The rework breaks that: a machine will be able to
  be renamed, re-addressed and replaced by a different one standing in for it, so a piece of
  identity taken now is no longer guaranteed to mean the same machine when it is read back.
  Before you touch it you have to know two things: how a machine's identity is established,
  changed and torn down today, and how far the change reaches - in particular every place
  that kept one of those pieces past the moment it had the machine itself, because those are
  the places that will silently point at the wrong machine, or at no machine, without a single
  line of them changing. Throughout, an answer that points at a place must give an exact
  file:line a teammate could jump straight to, plus one phrase on why it matters. A bare
  filename does not count, a set of names offered together with one shared reason and no
  location on any of them does not count, and a missed dependent is a regression shipped.

steps:
  - name: Map the server contract
    prompt: >
      Task: orient, and be thorough - the rest of the ticket is built on this. Start with the
      one thing everything else leans on: what identifies one of these machines, and where
      that identity is established, changed and destroyed. Trace it end to end. Show where the
      identifying fields are normalised as the record is written and where the previous value
      of the changing one is preserved; where a freshly created machine causes further records
      to be seeded from it, including any that take a COPY of an identifying field rather than
      a link back to it; where a lookup by identity is served out of a per-request cache
      instead of the database, and where that cache is emptied; and what the removal path does
      and does not clean up behind it. For each one give the file:line, the name of the
      routine it lives in, and one phrase on what it contributes. Then say, in a few
      sentences, what a rework of identity would have to preserve for everything already
      written down to keep meaning what it means today. A place named without the routine it
      lives in does not count, and neither does a routine named without the file:line where it
      is defined.
    checks:
      - type: response_richness
        value: "8"
        required: true
        description: The identity lifecycle traced through the routines that establish, change and tear it down, each located
      - type: mcp_tool_used
        value: sense_graph
        required: false
        layer: adoption

  - name: Audit every dependent of the server contract
    prompt: >
      Task: this is the core of the ticket, and you are working it with the budget the first
      part already cost you. Work it in two passes and give me both, in this order.
      FIRST PASS - the ground. Every place in this product that is handed one of these
      machines and works with it while it has it in front of it. All of them, organised by
      area, one line each, with the exact file:line and the routine that line sits in. I need
      that laid out in full before the second pass means anything, because the second pass is
      read against it: an area you summarised instead of listing reads as an area with nothing
      in it.
      SECOND PASS - and this is what the ticket turns on. Go back over that ground and past
      its edge, and find every place that KEPT something of a machine's identity after the
      machine itself was gone from its hands, and later trusts that keepsake to still mean the
      same machine when it comes back to it - a request later, a restart later, or in another
      system entirely. That trust is exactly what the rework withdraws, and nothing in such a
      place changes shape when it breaks. A place like that is often doing some other job
      altogether and may never be handed a machine at all; nothing on the line says a remote
      machine is involved, only that a value was kept and outlived the thing it was taken
      from. So for every one of them the answer has three parts: the exact file:line where
      that value is taken, written or read back, and the routine that line sits in; how long
      the value lives - inside one request, inside a stored record, or outside this product
      entirely; and one phrase on what this place starts getting wrong the first time the
      value no longer resolves to the machine it came from. Organise this pass by area too,
      one section per area, and treat an area as finished only when every place inside it is
      listed separately with its own location - if you cannot finish an area, say which one
      and say what you left in it. A file:line with no routine named around it does not count,
      a place named without saying what it kept does not count, and a missed one is a
      regression shipped.
    checks:
      - type: response_richness
        value: "6"
        required: true
        description: Every identity-keeping place located at file:line with what it kept, its lifetime and its own consequence
      - type: no_grep
        value: no_grep
        required: false
        layer: adoption
      - type: mcp_tool_used
        value: sense_blast
        required: false
        layer: adoption

scoring:
  weights:
    correctness: 0.7
    efficiency: 0.3

gold:
  # ---- ANCHORS: where identity is established, cached and torn down. Step 1's answer, and
  # ---- the map step 2 tells the agent to build first. Both arms reached all four in
  # ---- attempt 3 (contract 4/4 on both) and they do NOT score. Every line below was opened
  # ---- and read in this session. None of these four files appears in `dependents`.
  - id: contract-model
    group: contract
    match: [Models/Server.php]
    relation: "app/Models/Server.php:135 `protected static function booted()` - the identity lifecycle in one place: the saving hook preserves the old address at :147 `$payload['ip_previous'] = $server->getOriginal('ip');` when it changes, and the created hook at :157 seeds the settings row at :158, a destination at :170/:174, and then TWO stored variables that take a COPY of identity rather than a link - :191 `'key' => 'COOLIFY_SERVER_UUID'` with `'value' => $server->uuid,` at :192, and :199 `'key' => 'COOLIFY_SERVER_NAME'` with `'value' => $server->name,` at :200, both written once and never refreshed"
  - id: c:identity-map
    group: contract
    match: [Models/StandaloneDocker.php]
    relation: "app/Models/StandaloneDocker.php:135 `$server = Server::findCached($this->server_id);` inside `getServerAttribute(): ?Server` (def at :127, eager-loaded short-circuit at :130-:132) - the read side of identity: a stored integer is turned back into a machine through the per-request identity map declared at `app/Models/Server.php:131` `private static ?array $identityMapCache = null;` and served by `findCached()` at :230, filled at :241 and emptied only by `flushIdentityMap()` at :251; this is the mechanism every stored id in the product bottoms out in"
  - id: c:server-setting
    group: contract
    match: [Models/ServerSetting.php]
    relation: "app/Models/ServerSetting.php:59 `'server_id',` in the fillable list, with `public function server()` at :247 returning the belongsTo - the settings record created for every machine at `app/Models/Server.php:158`, the simplest example of identity kept as a link rather than as a copy"
  - id: c:server-delete
    group: contract
    match: [Server/Delete.php]
    relation: "app/Livewire/Server/Delete.php:60 `$this->server->delete();` inside `delete(...)`, followed at :61 by `DeleteServer::dispatch(` handed nine SCALARS across :62-:70 - the id at :62, the cloud-provider instance ids at :64/:68/:70, the token id at :65 and the team id at :66 - rather than the machine; the teardown path, and the point after which every piece of identity kept elsewhere refers to a machine that no longer exists"

  # ---- DEPENDENTS: twelve rows, ONE PER FILE, across eleven areas
  # ---- (app/Notifications/Container, app/Models, app/Livewire/Project/New,
  # ---- app/Livewire/Destination/New, app/Livewire, app/Livewire/Project/Shared,
  # ---- app/Livewire/Server/CaCertificate, app/Jobs,
  # ---- app/Livewire/Server/CloudProviderToken, app/Notifications/Server,
  # ---- app/Livewire/Server).
  # ---- Every row is in the shown `sense_blast` payload for `Server` quoted in the header,
  # ---- and every line below was opened and read in this session.
  # ---- Ten of the twelve carry a measured sense citation; none carries a baseline citation
  # ---- under an ask that excludes the near edge. Provenance per row is in the header.

  # -- a piece of identity copied into a message that leaves this product for a system we do
  # -- not control. The copy is taken at render time and is never revisited.
  - id: d:container-stopped
    group: dependents
    match: [Container/ContainerStopped.php]
    relation: "app/Notifications/Container/ContainerStopped.php:113 `'server_name' => $this->server->name,` with `'server_uuid' => $this->server->uuid,` at :114, inside the `$data` array opened at :108 in `toWebhook(): array` (def at :106) - an alert renders a machine's display name and handle into a payload posted to somebody else's endpoint; those keys are a contract other systems parse, so a rename makes every already-delivered alert refer to a machine nobody can find, and a stand-in machine makes them refer to the wrong one"
  - id: d:patch-check-link
    group: dependents
    match: [Server/ServerPatchCheck.php]
    relation: "app/Notifications/Server/ServerPatchCheck.php:19 `$this->serverUrl = base_url().'/server/'.$this->server->uuid.'/security/patches';` in `__construct(public Server $server, public array $patchData)` (def at :16, queued onto 'high' at :18) - the handle is baked into a deep link at construction time and stored in the `public string $serverUrl` declared at :14; the notification is queued, so the link is composed before delivery and then sits in somebody's mailbox indefinitely, pointing at whatever that handle resolves to when it is finally clicked"

  # -- a bare number filed into a stored row. The row outlives every process, and the line
  # -- that keeps it says nothing about a remote machine at all.
  - id: d:shared-env-var
    group: dependents
    match: [Models/SharedEnvironmentVariable.php]
    relation: "app/Models/SharedEnvironmentVariable.php:22 `'server_id',` in the fillable list, under the `// Type and relationships` comment at :17 and beside `'team_id',` :19 / `'project_id',` :20 / `'environment_id',` :21 - two rows of this table are created at `app/Models/Server.php:190` and `:198` whose stored VALUE is a copy of the machine's handle and display name, so this table holds identity twice over: once as a link a rename follows, and once as a value frozen at creation that it does not"
  - id: d:ssl-certificate
    group: dependents
    match: [Models/SslCertificate.php]
    relation: "app/Models/SslCertificate.php:16 `'server_id',` in the fillable list opened at :9, sitting between `'resource_id',` at :15 and `'common_name',` at :17 - a generated certificate is filed against the machine it was issued for, while the certificate material at :10-:11 is only valid where it was installed; the row survives the machine, so a re-used number hands one machine's private key to another"

  # -- a piece of identity carried through a redirect or a form step as a loose parameter,
  # -- then written into whatever gets created at the end of the flow.
  - id: d:new-resource-select
    group: dependents
    match: [New/Select.php]
    relation: "app/Livewire/Project/New/Select.php:441 `'server_id' => $this->server_id,` inside the `redirect()->route('project.resource.create', [` built at :436 in `setPostgresqlType(string $type)` (def at :432), and repeated at :456 in `whatToDoNext()` (def at :446) - the chosen machine survives the wizard as a bare number in a URL across a full browser round trip; nothing in this component holds a machine between steps, only the number does"
  - id: d:new-destination
    group: dependents
    match: [Destination/New/Docker.php]
